               {"text": "saheti :– sahayajñāḥ yajñasahitāḥ, prajāḥ trayo varṇāḥ, tāḥ, sṛṣṭvā utpādya, purā pūrvaṃ sargādau, uvāca uktavān, prajāpatiḥ prajānāṃ sraṣṭā, anena yajñena, prasaviṣyadhvaṃ prasavaḥ vṛddhiḥ utpattiḥ tāṃ kurudhvam. eṣaḥ yajñaḥ, vaḥ yuṣmākam, astu bhavatu, iṣṭakāmadhuk iṣṭān abhipretān kāmaphalaviśeṣān dogdhi iti iṣṭakāmadhuk.", "tr": "'Having created beings together with sacrifice…' Having created, brought forth, beings together with sacrifice — the three classes — in the beginning, at the start of creation, Prajāpati, the creator of beings, said: 'By this sacrifice shall you multiply' — bring about increase, birth. 'Let this sacrifice be for you the cow that yields your desires', the one that yields the particular fruits you desire."},
